                <pb facs="0701" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg507"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—No record has been found of the substance of the discussion at this meeting.
                        Brown’s diary entry for July 30,
                    however, contains the following reference to it: “… Met with communiqué
                    committee after Foreign Ministers, British and Soviets seemed to like draft.
                        Foote and I had prepared it. All of it
                    had previously been submitted to British. …”</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#superscript">3</hi>Sobolev
                    and Golunsky were the Soviet members of
                    this subcommittee (see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg399"
                        >p. 399</ref>), but it is not known who represented the Soviet Union at this
                    meeting.</p>
            </div>
